        "name": "recency-tiny-freq-depth",
        "retention_score": "last_access + log1p(frequency) * 2 + log1p(depth) * 1",
        "rationale": "The previous heavy frequency bonus (1000x) badly hurt performance because it kept stale but once-hot blocks over recently used ones, especially at tight capacities where LRU already does well. We keep recency as the overwhelming primary term and reduce frequency/depth to tiny tiebreakers: frequency adds at most ~14 for count 1e6 and depth adds at most ~14 for depth 1e6, so recency ordering dominates whenever there is any meaningful gap in last_access. This preserves pure-LRU behavior for sparse workloads while letting frequently reused, deep prefix blocks survive short idle gaps. Cheap: two log1p calls and simple arithmetic, well under the CPU limit (baseline runs ~1100 us max vs 50000 us budget)."
      },
