      "best_policy": {
        "name": "lru-soft-freq-no-depth",
        "retention_score": "last_access + log1p(frequency) * 30 + log1p(frequency) * 300 / (1 + (now - last_access) / 4000)",
        "rationale": "Parent hurt badly versus LRU: its raw depth*150 term dominated and forced many more evictions by over-retaining deep entries that were never reused, and its depth-free age penalty drove churn. New design keeps recency (last_access) as the primary signal like LRU, adds only a small unconditional frequency bonus (log1p(frequency)*30) for hot blocks, and a larger frequency bonus gated by recency (log1p(frequency)*300/(1+(now-last_access)/4000)) so strong frequency only boosts entries that were accessed reasonably recently. This decays with idle time without needing inserted_at, avoiding the parent's age penalty artifact that caused unnecessary eviction of freshly inserted cold tail entries. Removed depth entirely since empirically it increased extra tokens by over-protecting deep but rarely reused prefixes. Constants are cheap and small; expression is arithmetic plus one log1p, well within CPU feasibility (parent was ~3-5x LRU cost with depth and age terms). All terms bounded and denominators are >= 1 so no division by zero; intermediate values stay far below 1e12."
      },
